==============================================================================
WARNINGS ON THE CONCATENATED NOTICE AND LICENSE
==============================================================================

  1. SCOPE -- source release vs. convenience binaries
     The Apache release artifact of this repository is the SOURCE
     distribution: Dockerfiles, proxy sources, scripts and test material,
     all Apache-2.0. No third-party source code is vendored here; a scan of
     the tree found no non-ASF copyright header. Every component listed in
     NOTICE and LICENSE enters only the published CONTAINER IMAGES, which
     are convenience binaries assembled at build time from third-party base
     images and package repositories.
     CONSEQUENCE: a strict reading of ASF policy would keep the top-level
     LICENSE and NOTICE minimal (Apache-2.0 header only) and move this whole
     inventory to the images. The concatenated form used here is the more
     conservative disclosure. Confirm with the mentors which form the
     release is expected to carry.

  2. DUPLICATION AND DRIFT
     The concatenation repeats the same components many times, once per
     image, because the per-image files repeat them. Pekko does not repeat
     a block that applies to several modules; these files do, because the
     sources do and because deduplicating would mean rewriting them. It is
     a snapshot: it will drift as soon as any Dockerfile, requirements.in,
     package.json, composer.json or go.mod changes. Regenerate all three
     files with .licenses/concat-license-notice.sh whenever any per-image
     file changes. The per-image files -- not this concatenation -- remain
     authoritative for each image.

  3. INVENTORIES ARE NOT CLOSURES
     The component lists were derived from the declared dependencies in the
     build files, NOT from scanning a built image. The resolved transitive
     closures of pip, npm, composer and apt are substantially larger than
     what is listed. Before a release audit, run inside each built image:
       * Python : pip install pip-licenses && pip-licenses --format=plain
       * Node   : npm ls --all --long / license-checker
       * PHP    : composer licenses
       * Go     : go-licenses report ./...
       * Debian : dpkg-query -W -f='${Package} ${source:Package}\n'
     and reconcile the output with the per-image NOTICE and LICENSE.

  4. COPYRIGHT YEAR
     The NOTICE header still reads "Copyright 2024 The Apache Software
     Foundation". Update the year to the year of the release being cut.
     The year is carried verbatim from the per-image NOTICE files, so it
     must be changed there and the concatenation regenerated.

  5. NO FULL LICENSE TEXTS ARE INLINED
     The LICENSE sections name each third-party license (MIT, BSD-2/3,
     ISC, PSF, MPL-2.0, PHP-3.01, FTL, Info-ZIP, ...) and point to the
     package metadata directories inside each image instead of reproducing
     the texts. Pekko inlines the full text of every non-Apache license it
     depends on; this LICENSE does so only for Testify, whose text is in
     the tree as docs/LICENSE-testify.txt. This is acceptable only because
     none of the other code is in the source release (see warning 1). If
     any third-party source is ever vendored into this repository, its full
     license text MUST be added to LICENSE and its required attributions to
     NOTICE.

  6. DUAL LICENSES REQUIRE A RECORDED ELECTION
     Several components are dual-licensed and the per-image files state an
     election without a machine-readable record of it:
       * simplejson            MIT OR AFL-2.1        -- MIT elected
       * libfreetype6          FTL OR GPL-2.0+       -- FTL elected
       * python-dateutil       Apache-2.0 OR BSD-3   -- either is Category A
       * uv                    Apache-2.0 OR MIT     -- either is Category A
     gopkg.in/yaml.v3 is recorded as "Apache-2.0 AND MIT", a conjunction and
     not a choice; confirm that this is the intended reading and not a
     mis-stated "OR". Record all of these elections in the release
     documentation.

  7. CATEGORY B COMPONENTS
     ca-certificates (MPL-2.0) is Category B: it may ship in binary form
     only, unmodified, as a separate file, with the reciprocal license
     disclosed. It is used unmodified from the base image, which satisfies
     this, but the condition must not be broken by future changes.

  8. GPL IN THE BASE IMAGES
     Every runtime image inherits a GPL-licensed operating-system userland
     (glibc, coreutils, and for Java the OpenJDK class library under
     GPL-2.0 WITH Classpath-exception-2.0). These are Category X as
     bundled. They are disclosed, not redistributed in source form by the
     ASF. The Java images are the sharpest case: see the per-image WARN for
     runtime/java/* below, which recommends treating the JDK as an external
     base image the user pulls, or switching to Eclipse Temurin / Amazon
     Corretto.

  9. BUILD-TIME DOWNLOADS
     Components fetched from the network during the build (Google Gson from
     Maven Central for the Java images, uv from astral.sh for the Python
     images, npm and composer packages) are not in the source release but
     ARE redistributed inside the published images. They are disclosed in
     NOTICE and LICENSE. Any new build-time download must be added there.

 10. '*** SEE WARN ***' MARKERS
     The per-image NOTICE files announce that components incompatible with
     the Apache License 2.0 are flagged '*** SEE WARN ***'. Only two NOTICE
     files actually use the marker: experimental/php/v8.2 (libssl1.1) and
     experimental/python/v3.11cuda (CUDA, cuDNN, the Anaconda channel and
     the GCC toolchain). Every other NOTICE announces the convention and
     then flags nothing, recording the incompatible components in its WARN
     file instead. Either add the markers everywhere or drop the sentence,
     so the files do not promise a convention they do not use. Because
     NOTICE is concatenated verbatim, the unmet promise is repeated once
     per image.

 11. docs/ TREE
     docs/LICENSE.txt declares bundled Gradle wrapper files (gradlew,
     gradlew.bat, Apache-2.0) and Testify 1.2.1 (MIT), and
     docs/LICENSE-testify.txt carries the Testify text. Both are folded
     into the top-level LICENSE. Verify that gradlew/gradlew.bat are
     actually present in the release artifact; if they are not, remove the
     claim, and if they are, note that the Gradle wrapper JAR is a binary
     and binaries are not permitted in an ASF source release. Note also
     that docs/LICENSE.txt names Testify 1.2.1 while the proxy's go.mod
     resolves github.com/stretchr/testify v1.9.0: two different versions
     are disclosed for the same component. Reconcile them.

 12. DISCLAIMER
     The DISCLAIMER file at the repository root is required while the
     project is in incubation and must ship in every release artifact
     alongside LICENSE and NOTICE.

 13. PER-IMAGE BANNERS SURVIVE THE CONCATENATION
     Each block in LICENSE and NOTICE still opens with the banner of the
     file it came from ("Container image: apache/openserverless-runtime-..."),
     because those banners are part of the source text and removing them
     would be a rewrite. They are what identifies which image a block
     describes. Pekko names a module instead of an image at the head of
     each block; the effect is the same. Do not delete them without also
     deleting them from the per-image files.

 14. THE INCUBATING SUFFIX
     NOTICE names the product "Apache OpenServerless (Incubating)". Drop
     the suffix in the per-image files, and regenerate, only once the
     project has graduated.

 15. THE CUDA RUNTIME IS THE BLOCKING ITEM
     experimental/python/v3.11cuda is the most severe entry in this file
     and the only one that may not be resolvable by editing a Dockerfile.
     Its base image, pytorch/pytorch:2.5.1-cuda12.4-cudnn9-runtime, is
     chosen precisely for the proprietary NVIDIA CUDA 12.4 and cuDNN 9
     redistributables, which are Category X under the NVIDIA CUDA Toolkit
     EULA and the NVIDIA cuDNN Software License Agreement. Unlike the GPL
     userland inherited by every other image, these are not incidental:
     they are the reason the runtime exists, and they cannot be removed.
     The image additionally installs, and never removes, a GPL-3.0 build
     toolchain (build-essential, g++), and runs `conda install lxml`
     against the Anaconda default channel, whose Terms of Service are not
     an open source license. Those last two ARE inside the project's
     control and should be fixed regardless.
     This runtime is also not currently built: the Taskfile task
     build-experimental-runtime looks in runtime/experimental/{RT}/{VER}
     while the directory is experimental/python/v3.11cuda, so no image is
     produced or pushed. The Dockerfile is nevertheless in the SOURCE tree
     and therefore in the release artifact.
     DECIDE BEFORE THE RELEASE VOTE whether this runtime is revived, moved
     out of ASF infrastructure, or deleted. See its per-image WARN below.

 16. THE TOP-LEVEL DOCKERFILE IS THE ONE THAT IS ACTUALLY BUILT
     The Dockerfile at the repository root is now inventoried like every
     other image, from .licenses/root/. It had been the only Dockerfile in
     the tree with no per-image LICENSE, NOTICE or WARN, even though it is
     the one `task build-common` builds: the task's `dir:` line is
     commented out and it runs buildx from the toplevel. Three consequences
     for the concatenation, all detailed in .licenses/root/WARN below:
       * three blocks -- .licenses/root, common/common1.17.1 and
         common/common1.18.4 -- now describe what is in practice a single
         published image, openserverless-runtime-common, and none of them
         is banner'd with the tag that is actually pushed
         (1.18.4-<git tag>). The two Dockerfiles under common/ are not
         reached by any task, and common1.18.4's could not build
         standalone. Decide which is authoritative.
       * that image is PUSHED, so the GPL Debian userland of its golang
         base is inside a published ASF artifact. The two per-image WARN
         files under common/ describe it as a builder stage whose
         filesystem never ships; that is true of how the runtime images
         consume it, not of what buildx --push publishes.
       * the top-level Dockerfile copies DISCLAIMER, LICENSE and NOTICE but
         not WARN, unlike every other Dockerfile here, so the NOTICE inside
         that image refers to a WARN file the image does not contain.
     The third-party inventory in .licenses/root/LICENSE and NOTICE is
     byte-identical to common/common1.18.4's, because both build the same
     proxy from the same go.mod; that is duplication of the kind warning 2
     describes, and it is left in place rather than reconciled.


