==============================================================================
WARNINGS ON THE INVENTORY ITSELF
==============================================================================

  1. VERSION MISMATCH BETWEEN THIS DIRECTORY AND THE DOCKERFILE
     This directory is runtime/go/v1.25 and the image is published as
     apache/openserverless-runtime-golang:v1.25, but the Dockerfile builds
     FROM golang:1.26-bookworm and sets
     OW_EXECUTION_ENV=apacheopenserverless/runtime-golang-v1.26.
     LICENSE and NOTICE were written from what the Dockerfile actually
     pulls in (Go 1.26 on Debian bookworm), not from the directory name.
     Either the FROM line or the directory and tag are wrong; until that is
     resolved, the Go toolchain version named in LICENSE and NOTICE cannot
     be reconciled with the release coordinates of the image.

  2. FLOATING BASE IMAGE AND apt-get upgrade
     The base image is referenced by tag, not by digest, and the Dockerfile
     runs `apt-get update && apt-get upgrade -y`. The exact set of bundled
     operating-system packages therefore changes between builds of the same
     source tree. This inventory describes the components the Dockerfile
